# `npm run lint` is `prettier --check .`, over everything tracked except the
# paths below. Each block says what it holds and why it is not formatted.
# An entry here is a deliberate act: a new file conforms and needs no line.

# Generated, binary or vendored output. Never formatted.
dist/
node_modules/
public/
infra/
sprite-sources/
coverage/
.agent_specs/

# Written by `npm install`.
package-lock.json

# Generated assets and generated data: `npm run data:dex`, `npm run data:anil`,
# `npm run data:frlg:icons`, `npm run data:ui` and the `scripts/frlg/**`
# builders write these, so they are regenerated, never formatted.
src/assets/**
src/data/dex/**
src/data/frlg/**
src/data/anil/**
src/data/ui/**

# Regenerated by `npm run docs:coverage`, so it is generated output too.
docs/balance/effect-coverage.md

# The board's export and its derived tokens: `npm run design:export` and
# `npm run design:tokens` write these from Figma, so they are regenerated, never
# formatted (and `design/screens/**` carries the board's own raster for the diff).
design/frames/
design/screens/
design/tokens.json
design/board.json

# Packer and extraction scripts: plain Node ESM build tools, outside ESLint's
# linted set as well. They are left to the task that owns them.
scripts/**

# Prose and process documents. Prettier's markdown printer inserts blank lines
# around lists, realigns tables and rewrites `*emphasis*` to `_emphasis_`, so
# each of these would be genuinely rewritten: they are the docs tasks' and the
# Orchestrator's own files (CHANGELOG.md, TODO.md, docs/agent-ci.md), not lint
# targets.
AGENTS.md
CHANGELOG.md
TODO.md
docs/agent-ci.md
docs/art-direction.md
docs/balance/economy.md
docs/battle-spec.md
docs/data-spec.md
docs/design-spec.md
docs/maps-spec.md
docs/route-generator.md
docs/showdown-reuse.md
docs/tech-decisions.md
docs/tileset-spec.md
